<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zusho Hiromichi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1776–1849</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zusho Hiromichi was a retainer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma Domain</a> who restored its ruined finances from the late 1820s. He forced the domain's creditors among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osaka">Osaka</a> merchants to accept repayment of its huge debts over 250 years without interest, tightened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> monopoly in the Amami Islands and expanded trade through the Ryukyu Kingdom. His reforms gave Satsuma the wealth that later funded its modernisation; he died suddenly in 1849 amid a succession dispute.</p></div>
